sprdfb: skip the VT switch around suspend

On suspend the kernel moves to VT 63 and back. Xorg fbdev then re-enters
its VT with FBIOPUT_VSCREENINFO, which sprdfb rejects, and the server exits
(screen frozen, touch dead after waking). The panel needs no console
switch, so tell the PM core to skip it.

--- a/drivers/video/sprdfb/sprdfb_main.c
+++ b/drivers/video/sprdfb/sprdfb_main.c
@@ -211,6 +211,8 @@
 
 	fb->fbops = &sprdfb_ops;
 	fb->flags = FBINFO_DEFAULT;
+	/* Debian: no VT switch around suspend; Xorg fbdev cannot re-enter its VT on this panel */
+	fb->skip_vt_switch = true;
 
 	/* finish setting up the fb_info struct */
 	strncpy(fb->fix.id, "sprdfb", 16);
